{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall","id":779628,"title":"How to tell if someone is a Solar (e.g. the Manse at the centre of Whitewall).","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-04T02:03:17-08:00","id":779628,"title":"How to tell if someone is a Solar (e.g. the Manse at the centre of Whitewall).","content":"There are many examples throughout 1st and 2nd ed, where a device was made for the Solars and it takes an act almost legendary for the age to get to the point where anyone but a Solar can use the item (the Empress and the Realm Defense Grid), but have we ever gotten a baseline for how that mechanically works? Is it legit to say - this device can tell if you are a Solar or not? How much effort would a god have to go to, to fool it (the Syndics seem to not have that trick and they are pretty powerful, although it isn't in their purview to impersonate people).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T02:26:05-08:00","id":779634,"title":"","content":"It should require a solar anima or a dicepool beyond the standard range for gods and non-solar exalts. An especially skillfull, commited and dedicated dragonblood will still have a chance to do it, but it would be an exception, rather than the norm. At least this is what I imagine for a standard way to do it when a solar-only device is concerned.<br /> It can also have a requirement for someone of the lineage of the solar who created it or his dragonblood retinue in order for the device to be operated or it can have a &quot;trial by fire&quot; for any non-solar willing to wield the power of the device that is their either to test his virtues or his dedication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6865-nathaniel","name":"Nathaniel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T02:39:52-08:00","id":779638,"title":"","content":"I think it imlied the vrious Essence aspects were distinct on a fundamental levwl somehow, like the difference between the elementntal atoms of our world. They just dont work the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:10:54-08:00","id":779651,"title":"","content":"Solar Exalts can be recognised by Caste Marks and Anima Banners. Lunar, Sidereal, Abyssal, and Infernal(GSP) too. Terrestrial Exalts only have Anima Banners. Alchemical Exalts also have Anima Banners but their Caste Markings are the design style of their charm modules.<br /> <br /> Mostly its Caste Marks; they were basically meant to be an unforgeable Badges of Office. Anima banners were a little more personalised heraldric device.<br /> <br /> Obviously &quot;unforgeable&quot; is a relative term, as at least one Dragonblooded fooled a Solar-Only Manse/Artefact.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> In 2ed, different magical materials attuned easier for different exalt types; orichalcum responded best to Solar Exalts. You could <i>maybe</i> key some form of type-recognition on that basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 12-04-2015, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:26:22-08:00","id":779657,"title":"","content":"It's implied they are all different, but I've never seen a power which detects them, only mention of it in the writeup of plot level manses and devices. So trying to get a mechanical idea behind how it should work... what dice pool would you use to get around it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:32:11-08:00","id":779660,"title":"","content":"So the thing with dice pools/sux is that in this edition, Solars are no longer h flat out always best due to their dice cap. Lunars can fairly easily get a dice look of parity, and Sids can achieve more than Solars, for cheaper, with TN reduction. <br /> <br /> I would just fold it into needing a Solar anima display, personally. Having a &quot;you must be THIS tall to play&quot; dice pool requirement just doesn't work this edition. <br /> <br /> What's your goal with having a mechanical checkpoint as a prerequisite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:01:18-08:00","id":779678,"title":"","content":"...I'm personally hoping that this is mostly done away with, if only because it was extremely OVERused in 3e. &quot;Oh, Denandsor can only be fixed by a Solar.&quot; &quot;Oh, the Penitent can only be used with a Solar anima, unless you just want to burn the south and everyone in it to ash, in which case five DBs is enough, lol.&quot; &quot;Oh, Whitewall will only respond to a Solar.&quot;.<br /> <br /> If it comes back, I'd say shiny golden anima should be enough to force it, but a Sorcerous Working of adequate power ought to be able to bypass it, because it's stupid to have every other story locked behind golden swag.<br /> &quot;Why hasn't all this stuff been unlocked before now, then?&quot; Because sorcerous workings take time and effort which can be disrupted, be it Dragon-Blooded bringing a Wyld Hunt to stomp out the Lunar sorcerer trying to unlock the Tomb of the Golden Swag, or Sidereals subtly disrupting the Dragon-Blooded expedition because they really don't want Gorthak the Annihilator's grand war armor brought out of it, or Lunars sabotaging Sidereal plans because no thank you I don't want you doing whatever it is you're trying to do with this, because I'm like 97% sure it's bad for me and my plans.<br /> <br /> So basically, walking in, taking over, and utilizing the Penitent is a Story for a Solar circle and a good portion of a Chronicle for a Lunar, Dragon-Blooded, or Sidereal circle. or abyssals i guess but whatevs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 12-04-2015, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:18:56-08:00","id":779689,"title":"","content":"I really like the working idea. That system is just great for inserting a solution to lots of problems. That solution isn't cheap or quick but is still very rewarding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T05:44:46-08:00","id":779732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall?p=779660#post779660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your goal with having a mechanical checkpoint as a prerequisite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a framework that others agree is a reasonable bar for effort. I like the idea of a working being a solid workaround, maybe terrestrial for a one shot, celestial for a permanent?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T06:17:05-08:00","id":779745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall#post779628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it legit to say - this device can tell if you are a Solar or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; why would it not be?<br /> <br /> It's not really a mechanics thing, it's just a Storytelling thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T06:56:21-08:00","id":779767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall?p=779745#post779745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes; why would it not be?<br /> <br /> It's not really a mechanics thing, it's just a Storytelling thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a bit of a shorthand question, what I'm really interested in is what can then be used to cheat this question, and how difficult is it to create something which asks that question? Could a Solar Investigation or Occult charm do that test?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T07:41:24-08:00","id":779798,"title":"","content":"It could be as simple as 'the spirit has Measure the Wind and so can tell what are the people standing before it who want it to activate the device only it knows how to activate and which it is bound to do so only for a select sort of people.' Because in 3e Measure the Wind can tell apart different Exalt types. It's a good reason for Wyld Hunts to bring summoned demons with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T10:56:08-08:00","id":779946,"title":"","content":"Solars being the best at using artifacts is a fact of their being in 3e. You don't need to make an artifact that can magically detect whether a user is a Solar or not, you just need to make it so magically complex and powerful that only a Lawgiver could wield its might. It's noted that some truly exceptional Dragon-Blooded can tap into powers that are supposed to be Solar-exclusive, which neatly explains the Empress doing just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:19:13-08:00","id":779968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall?p=779946#post779946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars being the best at using artifacts is a fact of their being in 3e. You don't need to make an artifact that can magically detect whether a user is a Solar or not, you just need to make it so magically complex and powerful that only a Lawgiver could wield its might. It's noted that some truly exceptional Dragon-Blooded can tap into powers that are supposed to be Solar-exclusive, which neatly explains the Empress doing just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hilariously, this makes Dragon-Blooded better with Artifacts at times than Lunars and Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:51:39-08:00","id":780000,"title":"","content":"I've always just figured that the actual, functional Essence produced by different Exalt Types was subtly different. It explains why different MMs synthesize better with different Exalt Types (that material is just more compatible with the vagaries of your Essence). And, this is backed up by the books with how manses work. A Solar-aspected demense is a Solar-aspected demense, and you have to build a Solar-aspected Manse on top of it...and this is because the Essence that has pooled around the demense is Solar-aspected, and so behaves differently than other types of Essence. So, Solars generate Solar-aspected Essence. Just like how a Solar manse needs a Solar demense to sit on top of in order to function...and might explode if you build it on the wrong sort of demense...it should be possible to create other things that require Solar-aspected Essence in order to function.<br /> <br /> Another source of 'Only Solars can do this' is to make it require Solar-Circle Sorcery to repair it exactly as it was. Sans the Mantle of Brigid in the hands of a Lunar or Siddie...that just isn't happening without a Solar.<br /> <br /> Of course, 2E laid out methods by which the aspect of a demense could be changed...and this is described as a very slow and work-intensive process the time-period of which is measured in years. It also, apparently, ruins any connection to a manse sitting on it...because manse construction is a VERY specialized process. But they also talked about the ability to remodel a manse to accommodate for minor changes to the demense it sits upon...meaning that if you very gradually were to change the demense, you could possibly remodel the manse to keep up with the change in power-source. The real challenge is that doing this can change the effects and powers of the manse...which is not generally something you want to do.<br /> <br /> So...using that as a mental template...here's the thinking. It is possible to remodel an artifact, manse, or other system to accept a different power source by several possible means.<br /> <br /> With a complex artifact (pretty much required to get something that will only work for a Solar), it may be possible to take some long-running Craft (Artifice) rolls to first understand how the artifact works, and then remodel it to allow some other aspect of Essence to power it. Unfortunately, this may cause the Artifact's capabilities to change somewhat to be more in-line its new Aspect. The Artificer should be able determine what will change in advance...and possibly up the difficulty to reduce the impact of these changes. A 'simple' artifact like a Daiklave is not complicated enough to be successfully altered in this way.<br /> <br /> With a manse...well, same idea, but with Geomancy instead. You make long-running roles to change the aspect of the Demense...and roles with similar rules to change the aspect of the Manse. The problem is that you have to convert both the demense and the manse to the new aspect at the same speed. If one finishes before the other, or you botch rolls...you've got serious problems...like boomy manse-explody problems.<br /> <br /> And finally, with Sorcery...it is possible to conduct a Sorcerous Working against a target to 'hack it' into working. This, bolstered by the strongest fate the Sidereals could weave for her, coupled with the death of her entire squad (possibly as sacrifices, if you want to say so), and a good bit of plain-old luck, is how Her Redness got the Realm Defense Grid up and running. The catch is...'hacking' an artifact system into working in a way it is not designed to is a touchy prospect at best. I'd have to think about it a bit...but the higher rated the system you were trying to alter, the higher Circle/Ambition I would make trying to perform a seamless 'hack job.' By accepting limitations on your hack job, you could reduce the difficulty...so, basically, the 'weird behavior' that comes from messing up Working rolls...you can take ones intentionally to make the hack easier...though, like with messed up Working rolls, the ST has say on what exactly the problem is.<br /> <br /> So, yes...the Scarlet Empress managed to get the Sword of Creation to work...but it won't work for any Terrestrial except her...it exacts a much greater toll on her (higher Essence charge? maybe inflicts damage of some sort?) to use it...and it doesn't really work right, setting off local disasters in addition to the carnage it unleashes on her targets and everything near them...as opposed to the terrifyingly lethal precision it operates with when in the hands of a Solar. In fact, these 'issues' it has are of sufficient concern that she didn't just hold back from using it for fear of wrecking her new empire...but also because she had no idea how bad the disasters would be each time...perhaps next time a disaster may be bad enough to cripple the RDG...and honestly...no one has any idea how to fix this thing if it breaks. And to address the 'drawbacks' from her working...the reason those drawbacks are so relatively minor are because of the absurdly good luck that the Sidereals gave her while weaving basically everything left in Creation into making her succeed.<br /> <br /> (In my head...the RDG is composed of a ton of different manses, a big pile of N/A Artifacts all wired into a single system, and a heap of high ambition Solar Workings...probably assembled by basically every Solar (and possibly Lunar and Sidereal) Craftsman alive at the time. Makes it quite a bit more epic as the crown jewel of the weapons of the First Age.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3937,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","user":"guildsbounty","date":". 12-04-2015, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:37:24-08:00","id":780052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall?p=779968#post779968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hilariously, this makes Dragon-Blooded better with Artifacts at times than Lunars and Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just at times. They're the second best artifact users in the game now, it's one of their schticks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T00:14:06-08:00","id":780430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall?p=779798#post779798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be as simple as 'the spirit has Measure the Wind and so can tell what are the people standing before it who want it to activate the device only it knows how to activate and which it is bound to do so only for a select sort of people.' Because in 3e Measure the Wind can tell apart different Exalt types. It's a good reason for Wyld Hunts to bring summoned demons with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't just people standing in front of it, there's usually some form of limit to Measure the Wind. Blood Apes need to taste the blood of the person they are Measuring, for example. The charm also isn't free, and only targets one person at a time. It isn't a DBZ scouter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T02:55:19-08:00","id":780465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall?p=779968#post779968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hilariously, this makes Dragon-Blooded better with Artifacts at times than Lunars and Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't that intentional? Weren't DB's supposed to be second-best at evocations? (Possibly setting aside Alchies, who are probably only a conceptual glimmer ATM)<br /> <br /> Rather than strict tiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T05:25:34-08:00","id":780515,"title":"","content":"DBs being more &quot;natural&quot; with artefacts than Celestial Exalted seems like it could be within in intent. I think YMMV on this question - is Terrestials being better with artefacts than the two Celestial Exalted, hilarious or &quot;What's the joke?&quot;? - can depend on how powerful you see artefacts and craft as being. <br /> <br /> If using and understanding artefacts is the allpower on which everything builds (effectively, there is a tiering system and you gauge it by how good you are at making and using artefacts), then, well, yes, kind of hilarious for Dragonbloods to be better with them than Celestial Exalted. <br /> <br /> If artefacts more of a &quot;A nice channel to go down, but not that essential for true power and flexibility&quot; (for one example, sorcerous workings can achieve a lot without much Craft) thing then perhaps it's more &quot;What's the joke?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T08:45:47-08:00","id":780567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall?p=780465#post780465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Isn't that intentional? Weren't DB's supposed to be second-best at evocations? (Possibly setting aside Alchies, who are probably only a conceptual glimmer ATM)<br /> <br /> Rather than strict tiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant it was funny in a good way. I know it's intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T17:51:10-08:00","id":780824,"title":"","content":"The easy way, in 2e, to tell if someone was a Solar or not... throw magical cupcakes at him. <br /> <br /> If he could perfect them more or less indefinitely, he's probably a Solar and you should stop throwing them and apologize before he kills you. <br /> <br /> If he can't perfect the cupcakes because they're magical and thus dies in one hit, he's a Dragon-Blooded. <br /> <br /> If he perfects them until he runs out of Willpower or suffers a Resonance eruption (and then dies in one hit), he's an Abyssal. <br /> <br /> If he eats all your cupcakes, he's a Lunar. <br /> <br /> And if he vanishes and you forget why you were throwing cupcakes, he's a Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-06-2015, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T18:16:12-08:00","id":780839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall?p=780824#post780824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if he -redacted-, he's a -redacted-.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you.<br /> <br /> ...What were we talking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T08:17:56-08:00","id":781700,"title":"","content":"You could exploit their capacity to heal ? If you start branding travelers/citizens/etc, most of the people are going to walk around with a tell tale scar. Solars, among other people with supernatural recuperation, will quickly get over that little blemish. From there you know you've got someone out of the ordinary ! To keep the convolution going, take your freshly healed suspect and shake them until they get upset enough to use charms and you see something sparkly. It's a fairly foolproof method ... that or the other thing ... foolish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T08:52:58-08:00","id":781714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/779628-how-to-tell-if-someone-is-a-solar-e-g-the-manse-at-the-centre-of-whitewall?p=781700#post781700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could exploit their capacity to heal ? If you start branding travelers/citizens/etc, most of the people are going to walk around with a tell tale scar. Solars, among other people with supernatural recuperation, will quickly get over that little blemish. From there you know you've got someone out of the ordinary ! To keep the convolution going, take your freshly healed suspect and shake them until they get upset enough to use charms and you see something sparkly. It's a fairly foolproof method ... that or the other thing ... foolish.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you aren't a Solar, I'm pretty sure your capacity to see through any disguise they might put up to make it look like they still have the scar will invalidate this strategy... and piss off a lot of people who are at least as powerful as you.<br /> <br /> Also, scars / brands are normally seen as agg / crippling damage, which by default they don't heal quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T11:12:41-08:00","id":781759,"title":"","content":"maybe the manse has instructions to enter on the door that can only be seen with Eyes of the Unconquered Sun??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}